With GitHub:
•	Everyone has their own copy to work on
•	All changes are saved and tracked
•	If someone makes a mistake, you can easily undo it
•	You can see who contributed each recipe
1. Repository ("Repo")
•	What it is: A project folder that contains all your files
•	Simple terms: Your digital project notebook
•	Example: "Family-Cookbook" folder containing all recipes
2. Commit
•	What it is: Saving a snapshot of your work
•	Simple terms: Taking a photo of your progress
•	Example: "Saved version with 10 new recipes added"
